---- ENDF/B-VIII.1    MATERIAL 3011         REVISION 1            3011 1451
----- THERMAL NEUTRON SCATTERING DATA                             3011 1451
------ ENDF-6                                                     3011 1451
                                                                  3011 1451
  Temperatures = 293.6 400 500 600 700 800 1000 1200 K            3011 1451
                                                                  3011 1451
 HISTORY                                                          3011 1451
 -------                                                          3011 1451
 This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction Physics  3011 1451
 (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University (USA). Eight     3011 1451
 temperatures are available in this library. The inelastic        3011 1451
 scattering cross section libraries for Ca in stoichiometric CaH2 3011 1451
 were developed using ab initio lattice dynamics (AILD) [1,2]. The3011 1451
 Full Law Analysis Scattering System Hub (FLASSH) was used to     3011 1451
 produce MT = 2 (compound coherent) and MT = 4 data [3]. This is a3011 1451
 novel evaluation in the ENDF/B library; by convention, MAT=3011  3011 1451
 and ZA=3111 are chosen for Ca in CaH2.                           3011 1451
                                                                  3011 1451
 THEORY                                                           3011 1451
 ------                                                           3011 1451
 CaH2 has an orthorhombic crystal structure belonging to the Pnma 3011 1451
 Hermann-Mauguin space group (#62), with three nonequivalent atom 3011 1451
 sites. One nonequivalent site belongs to the metal ion, while the3011 1451
 other two both contain hydrogen atoms. As a result, these        3011 1451
 hydrogen atoms provide distinct contributions to the overall     3011 1451
 frequency spectrum of the material and thus have different       3011 1451
 thermal scattering cross sections. An evaluation has been        3011 1451
 submitted for each nonequivalent hydrogen atom in CaH2, in       3011 1451
 addition to this evaluation for the metal ion. The coherent      3011 1451
 elastic cross section is stored on the calcium tape and includes 3011 1451
 contributions from all nonequivalent sites (compound coherent).  3011 1451
 The incoherent elastic cross section of calcium is negligible and3011 1451
 therefore incoherent elastic scattering by Ca is ignored.        3011 1451
 Experimental lattice data was used in the calculation of the     3011 1451
 coherent elastic cross section [4]. The total isotopic free atom 3011 1451
 cross sections are taken from MF = 3, MT = 2 of the ENDF/B-VIII.03011 1451
 nuclide evaluations [5] at 1.0E-05 eV for all isotopes except    3011 1451
 Ca-46. For this calcium isotope, the total free atom cross       3011 1451
 section listed in the ENDF/B-VIII.0 nuclide evaluation resulted  3011 1451
 in physical inconsistencies in the low-energy region of the cross3011 1451
 sections of natural calcium. Therefore the value of the total    3011 1451
 free atom cross section used in this evaluation for Ca-46 was    3011 1451
 obtained from the NIST database [6], which was the next best     3011 1451
 available data. The incoherent free atom cross sections for all  3011 1451
 isotopes were likewise obtained from the NIST database, while the3011 1451
 coherent free atom cross sections were calculated by subtracting 3011 1451
 the incoherent values from the total free atom values. The       3011 1451
 coherent free atom cross sections were converted to coherent free3011 1451
 atom scattering lengths in order to account for the negative     3011 1451
 scattering length of hydrogen in the calculation of the coherent 3011 1451
 elastic scattering cross section of the compound. In this same   3011 1451
 calculation, H-1 as opposed to naturally-weighted H is used.     3011 1451
